(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff RTD temperature sensor channel process image.
</summary>
<description>
Represents the standard 16-bit status plus INT16 measured-value PDO, not the compact value-only PDO.
Default temperature presentation is 0.1 deg C per digit; high resolution is 0.01 deg C per digit.
Thus raw 253 means 25.3 or 2.53 deg C respectively. Configure presentation explicitly.
Signed-amount or resistance presentations require their matching interpretation; this type stores raw bits.
Check channel status before using Value. This record does not choose or convert device presentation.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE RTD_INPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
	Value AT %I* : INT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
